lesson: 125
title: The missing number in a story
level: primary-1
stars: 1
explain: Sometimes a story hides one number: what there was at first, or how many were added or taken. The whole and one part are known.
explain: The missing part is the whole minus the known part. Some apples and 5 more make 12: □ + 5 = 12, so □ = 12 − 5 = 7.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing w=8..60 p=2..40
need: w - p >= 2
answer: w - p
exercise: {a} had some {t}. {b} gave {a.him} {p} more. Now {a} has {w} {t}. How many {t} did {a} have at first?
exercise: {a} had {w} {t}. {a.He} gave some to {b} and has {p} {t} left. How many {t} did {a.he} give to {b}?
exercise: {a} had {p} {t}. After {b} gave {a.him} some more, {a} had {w}. How many {t} did {b} give?
exercise: I think of a number. When I add {p} to it, I get {w}. What is my number?
exercise: There were some {t} in a box. {a} put in {p} more, and now there are {w} {t} in the box. How many {t} were in the box before?
test: What number goes in the box: □ + {p} = {w}?
test: {w} − □ = {p}. What is the missing number?
test: {a} baked {w} cookies. After eating some of them with friends, {a.he} has {p} cookies left. How many cookies were eaten?
test: {b} is collecting {t}. With {p} more {t}, {b} would have exactly {w}. How many {t} does {b} have now?
exercise: {a} had some {t}. {b} gave {a.him} another {p}, and now {a} has {w}. How many {t} did {a} start with?
exercise: {a} had {w} {t}, handed some to {b}, and still has {p}. How many {t} did {b} get?
exercise: After {b} gave {a} some {t}, {a} had {w}. Before that {a} had {p}. How many {t} did {b} give {a}?
exercise: I am thinking of a number. If I add {p}, I get {w}. What number am I thinking of?
exercise: Some {t} were in a box in a classroom in Nottingham. {a} added {p} more, making {w} in all. How many {t} were in the box at first?
exercise: {a} needs {w} {t} for a school fair in Georgia. {a.He} already has {p}. How many more {t} does {a.he} need?
exercise: What number plus {p} makes {w}?
exercise: {a} gave away some of {a.his} {w} {t} and has {p} remaining. How many did {a.he} give away?
test: Fill in the blank: {p} + __ = {w}.
test: {w} take away what number leaves {p}?
test: A bakery in Halifax made {w} muffins. By closing time {p} muffins were left. How many muffins were sold?
test: {b} wants {w} stamps for {b.his} album. {b.He} has {p} so far. How many stamps are still missing?
test: {w} children are on a school trip in Perth. {p} of them are boys. How many are girls?
test: A bus in Cork left a stop with {w} passengers after {p} got on there. How many passengers were on the bus before that stop?
exercise: had some {t}, {b} gave me {p}, now got {w}. how many i have at first
exercise: {a} had {w} {t}, gave {b} some, {p+1} left, no wait, {p} left. how many {a.he} give
exercise: {b} reckons □ + {p} = {w} means □ is {w+p}. nah that's wrong, what's □
exercise: {a} needs {w} {t} for the fair, got {p} already, fair starts at 9 btw. how many more {a.he} need
test: {w} minus what makes {p}
test: bakery made {w} muffins, {p+2} left, sorry, {p} left at closing. how many sold
test: {a} says {p} + __ = {w} so __ = {w} + {p} = {w+p}. that's wrong innit, whats the blank
exam: It is given that {a}, upon receipt of {p} {t} from {b}, holds {w} {t} in total. Determine the number of {t} originally in the possession of {a}.
exam: Whereas {a} held {w} {t} and, following a transfer of an unspecified quantity thereof to {b}, retains {p} {t}, ascertain the quantity so transferred.
exam: A collection of {p} {t} was augmented by a contribution from {b}, whereupon it comprised {w} {t}. State the magnitude of the said contribution.
exam: Compute the unknown number which, when increased by {p}, yields {w}.
exercise: After the old dog was put down, the family gave its biscuits to the neighbours' dog. They had {w} biscuits and now have {p} left. How many biscuits did they give away?
exercise: Uncle Joe passed away and left {a} some {t}. Then {b} gave {a} {p} more, and now {a} has {w} {t}. How many {t} did Uncle Joe leave?
test: {a}'s "a little short" this week, borrowed some off me. i had {w} dollars, now i got {p}. how much did {a.he} take, cheeky sod
